## 3. Process map
A  CERAMIC FACES blank → sinter → grind OML / IML → densify IML → coat-fire → overcoat → NDE → bag
B  HEMP CORES lot bake → degum → form → impregnate → layup → cure → post-cure → net CNC → edge seal → outgas bake → NDE → bag
C  BACKING + DOUBLER cut BK-SG → bond / co-cure DBL-TI → install INS-TI → drill S1–S4 from jig → NDE
D  PLATE BOND dry-fit on chest master → ADH-F ceramic↔core↔backing → cure → NDE → serial
E  CUP machine wall → liner → aft W layer → SG wrap → leak / thermal coupon → cap
F  HARNESS SPIDER machine / weld / bond nodes → proof 2× Case A → prime / isolate
G  CHEST MATE HUT dummy or flight HUT → spider on Datum A/B → plates hung → cup torqued → cap → harness-to-dorsal lines → leak / electrical / proof → bag ASSY-CHEST

A, B, C can run in parallel. D waits on A+B+C. G waits on D+E+F.

---

## 4. Stream A — ceramic faces

1. Cut / mold oversize blanks. One blank per facet. Chest set is a family; do not mix lots across a plastron.
2. Sinter to the ceramic spec. Record kiln curve.
3. Grind OML to the facet (triangle language, sharp but not knife-edge). Grind IML flat to bond spec.
4. Densify IML (CER-D). This is the Shuttle lesson. Skip it and the adhesive lets go.
5. Coat-fire CER-B (black) on OML. Chest is mostly black leading surface.
6. CER-WP waterproof / AO overcoat.
7. NDE: visual, mass, tap, coating thickness, edge chips.
8. Bag with foam dams. Ceramic chips are scrap, not “fit on the side.”

Chest-specific: the plastron face that receives CAP-S is a closeout ring, not a continuous tile. Leave the 118 mm land uncoated on the IML so the cap seal sees a known surface.

---

## 5. Stream B — hemp cores (chest cutouts included)

Follow the hemp-core traveler. Chest deltas only:

1. CORE-LOT bake #1 / degum / bake #2 as standard.
2. Forms: HEMP-W skins + HEMP-U on the S1–S4 land (still no bolt in the hemp) + HEMP-M fill to 6–10 mm.
3. Impregnate Route A prepreg preferred.
4. Layup on a chest caul that already has the 118 mm plug. Core must stop at the sealed land. Do not fill the bore with bast.
5. Cure + post-cure.
6. CNC net, including inner bore +3 mm for the seal stack.
7. Edge-seal **outer perimeter and inner bore**. 10×: no fuzzy fiber.
8. Vacuum bake #3 to TML / CVCM gate.
9. NDE + coupons from the same bag.
10. Bag, desiccant, serial. If the humidity indicator trips, re-bake. Do not bond a wet chest core.

Warp: call it on the drawing. Typical chest: warp vertical on the large center facets.

---

## 6. Stream C — backing and doubler

1. Cut BK-SG to net + bond flash.
2. Bond or co-cure DBL-TI (or DBL-SG if you need dielectric near HV).
3. Install INS-TI inserts. Captive. No spinning nuts on EVA.
4. Drill S1–S4 and the 6 mm pin from a steel jig locked to Datum A/B. Do not drill from the ceramic.
5. Tap / inspect threads. A286 or Ti M8 only.
6. Peel-ply or abrade the core-facing side to the ADH-F spec.
7. NDE: insert pull coupon on a witness piece from the same cure.

The doubler is the bolt land. The core is not.

---

## 7. Stream D — plate bond (the sandwich)

1. Pull ceramic, core, backing from dry bags. Moisture gate on the core.
2. Dry-fit the whole chest family on the chest master (HUT dummy + spider). Check:
   - facet gaps / overlap (Iron Man scale language)
   - 118 mm land concentric to the cup
   - no core proud of the seal land
   - step/gap within drawing
3. ADH-F ceramic IML → core, 0.15–0.25 mm. If you are outside that window, stop.
4. ADH-F core → backing.
5. Bag or fixture-cure per adhesive. Caul the OML so facets stay coplanar.
6. Trim flash. Do not nick the ceramic coat.
7. NDE: tap, thermography or UT at the bond, visual step/gap, mass.
8. Serial PLT-CHEST-xxx and lock it to CORE-LOT + CER lot + ADH lot.

Do not hang plates on the flight HUT until Stream F is proofed.

---

## 8. Stream E — sternum cup (ABH-2600-SM)

1. Machine CUP-TI or CUP-IN wall: OD 118 mm class, ID for 72 mm clear + liner.
2. Bond / shrink CUP-CU liner (1.0–1.5 mm).
3. Apply CUP-W (2–4 mm W or W-Cu) on the **aft / crew side only**.
4. Wrap CUP-SG (S-glass / PI, 2 mm) on the outer wall.
5. Machine flange for S1–S4 pattern. Same jig as Stream C.
6. Install COOL-A/B jacket passages and QDs.
7. Install TM bosses (thermistors, optional dose).
8. Fit CAP-S: ceramic-faced, faceted, removable. Optional V-EBM latch on the cap — vacuum-side only, HV inhibited in air / dirty vac.
9. Leak-check cup (helium or pressure decay).
10. Thermal coupon: 150 W continuous / 400 W peak analog into the liner; crew-side wall ≤ 80 °C with loop on.
11. Bag CUP-SM-xxx. No hemp, no ceramic chips, no “Rs feed” fitting anywhere on this part.

---

## 9. Stream F — chest harness spider

This is the chest half of the harness, not the full dorsal pack.

1. Cut / machine EXO-TI or EXO-IN nodes:
   - four sternum ears (S1–S4)
   - two superior runs toward the hatch ring (mate to FTL-BH-1 upper bolts)
   - two inferior runs toward the pelvic yoke
   - optional lateral runs under the pauldrons (no plate attach)
2. Join: weld, bolt, or co-bond per the drawing. Stress-relieve if welded.
3. Isolate: PI / S-glass where the spider can see PWR-HV creepage.
4. Proof: 2 × Case A (6 g axial equivalent on the chest mass properties, including 8 kg SM analog). Hold. No yield, no cracked joint.
5. Fit-check on Datum A/B/C. Pin hole must pick up without a mallet.
6. Prime / conversion coat. No bare steel.
7. Serial HARN-CH-xxx.

Strap option (donning aid only): textile secondary over the spider. Textile does not carry Case A.

---

## 10. Stream G — chest mate (the article)

Tool: HUT dummy first. Flight HUT only after dummy pass.

1. Locate HARN-CH on Datum A/B. Pin, then S1–S4 into the HUT lattice — still no plates.
2. Torque S1–S4 to spec in star pattern. Witness marks.
3. Hang PLT-CHEST family from backing inserts onto the spider / HUT lands. Ceramic is a passenger.
4. Confirm inner bore is clear. Drop CUP-SM from the front or from the interior per drawing. Flange seats on the doubler, not on hemp.
5. Torque cup flange. Same star pattern. Cap off.
6. Route COOL-A/B and DSH-HP stub aft along the superior longerons to the hatch ring. Bellows at the ring. No line across a plate bond.
7. Mate PWR-1 and TM. Dead-face half stays on the harness side.
8. If V-EBM cap latch is fitted: hook HV only at the inhibit box. Do not energize in the shop air without the Paschen procedure.
9. LCVG stand-off: 8–15 mm, no hard cup-to-sternum contact.
10. Checks before bag:
    - pressure-shell leak (if on flight HUT)
    - cup leak
    - loop flow / ΔT at 150 W analog
    - insulation resistance PWR-1
    - HV inhibit proves open
    - visual step/gap on every chest facet
    - no hemp visible at the bore
11. Serial ASSY-CHEST-xxx. Photograph OML + inner lands. Bag.

Dorsal pack (FTL-BH-1 / DSH-1) mates at the hatch ring on a separate traveler. This chest article must accept that pack without pulling a plate.

---

## 11. Don / doff and swap times (acceptance)

| Action | Gate |
|---|---|
| Cap off, module out (SM analog) | ≤ 90 s on a stand |
| Full cup off | plates stay on |
| One chest plate off | adjacent plates stay; no cup movement |
| Harness undock (dorsal) | PWR-1 and HV dead-face, COOL QDs shut |

If you have to unbond a sandwich to change the cup, the design failed Stream G.

---

## 12. Inspection gates (copy onto the traveler)

| Gate | Stream | Fail if |
|---|---|---|
| CER coat + IML densify | A | Chip, bare substrate, no densify record |
| Core moisture + edge seal | B | Indicator trip, fuzzy bore |
| S1–S4 from jig | C / F | Pattern mismatch > drawing |
| ADH-F thickness | D | Outside 0.15–0.25 mm |
| Cup leak + 80 °C wall | E | Leak or over-temp at 150 W |
| Spider 2 × Case A | F | Yield, cracked node |
| Step/gap + no hemp in bore | G | Core proud, plate clash |
| Genealogy complete | G | Any lot blank |

---

## 13. Failure modes this traveler exists to prevent

| Skip | Result |
|---|---|
| Densify IML | Ceramic pops on the first thermal cycle |
| Edge-seal the bore | Chest core pumps into the cup land |
| Bolt in ceramic or hemp | Crush + leak + a plate you cannot pull |
| Mix CORE-LOTs on one plastron | Untestable bond family |
| Proof spider after plates are hung | You just acoustic-tested tiles with a hammer |
| Coolant across a plate bond | First flex shears a line and a sandwich |
| REAL-core mass in the cup | 132 g + 176 g tide — FAIL-CLOSED, not a process step |
| Energize V-EBM in air | Paschen arc |

---

## 14. First article (one chest, not a suit)

1. Three-facet plastron + one collateral scale.
2. One core with bore, one without.
3. One cup, one spider, dummy HUT.
4. Coupons: ceramic bond flatwise, core shear, cup leak, spider proof.
5. Mate, 150 W thermal, 2 × Case A on the dummy, cap swap in 90 s.
6. Freeze the recipe. Then cut a full chest family.

Title-block notes:
- ABH-2600-SM only in the cup.
- ABH-2600-REAL is not this traveler.
- FTL-BH-1 is the dorsal service pack; superluminal function is not a shop step.
- Ice lines, if any, terminate on the pack / bus, not at Rs.